{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleReciprocity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleReciprocity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleReciprocity.dual_lt_of_y_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleReciprocity.dual_lt_of_y_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ModularDoubleReciprocity.lean#L149-L162","doc":"**Near `1` is the worst place to sit.** For `0 < y < 1` the dual's log is\nstrictly the more negative, so `|q~| < |q|`; by `logQDual_eq_div` the gap widens\nreciprocally as `y → 0`.\n\nThe substrate has `y = ln q0 / (2pi) ≈ 0.0166`, which is this case — and the\nresulting `|log q~| ≈ 378` is the `4.8e-165`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleReciprocity.self_dual_iff_y_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleReciprocity.self_dual_iff_y_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ModularDoubleReciprocity.lean#L131-L147","doc":"**The balanced point.** The two sides agree exactly at `y = 1` — at `c = 2pi`\nthat is `q = exp(-2pi) ≈ 0.00187`.\n\nArchimedean: the `↔` needs `y > 0` to rule out `y = -1`, so this one takes `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleReciprocity.logQDual_eq_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleReciprocity.logQDual_eq_div","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ModularDoubleReciprocity.lean#L119-L129","doc":"The dual through the reciprocity: `log q~ = c^2 / log q`.\n\nReciprocal, so the suppression is not gradual — halving `|log q|` doubles\n`|log q~|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleReciprocity.modular_reciprocity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleReciprocity.modular_reciprocity","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ModularDoubleReciprocity.lean#L104-L117","doc":"**The modular-double reciprocity.** `log q * log q~ = c^2`, for every\n`y ≠ 0` — the `y` cancels.\n\nGeneric per §7c: any field, and no `pi`, no ordering, no `ℝ`.\n\nThis is a statement about the two `def`s above, which are stipulated. It is\n`(c y)(c / y) = c^2` and nothing more. That it is *algebraic* is the Option-B\npoint — an algebraic identity leaves no convention to re-choose — but the step\nfrom Faddeev's `q`, `q~` to these definitions is imported, not proved. See the\nmodule docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleReciprocity.logQDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleReciprocity.logQDual","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ModularDoubleReciprocity.lean#L100-L102","doc":"`log q~` for the modular dual `q~ = exp(-2 pi i / b^2)` with `b^2 = i y`:\nequals `-(c / y)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleReciprocity.logQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleReciprocity.logQ","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ModularDoubleReciprocity.lean#L96-L98","doc":"`log q` for `q = exp(2 pi i b^2)` with `b^2 = i y`, in units where `c = 2pi`:\nequals `-(c * y)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}